{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqatxdyv38f","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","item":"CRITICAL CONSTRAINT: state is REASSIGNED not just mutated (let state = ... at /reset line 1386 and partially /workspace line 1438). Route modules therefore CANNOT capture state at construction. ctx must expose LIVE access via a holder (e.g. ctx.core.state accessor), or reads go stale after a reset.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-12T11:14:39.227Z"}
{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqatxdyv38f","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","item":"Auth is centralized: protectedPath prefix matching (daemon.js ~1350) runs ONCE before routing. Keep it in the daemon.js shell; route modules must NOT each re-auth.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-12T11:14:39.227Z"}
{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqatxdyv38f","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","item":"Route bodies are order-independent among themselves: matches are exact p === '/...' equality, so grouping/reordering bodies is safe. Only the final fall-through (/ static html + 404) must remain last.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-12T11:14:39.227Z"}
{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqatxdyv38f","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","item":"Shared helpers route modules need via ctx: send, sendOp (opCache idempotency layer), readBody, notifyChange (SSE + respCache clear), buildGraph, plus per-module lib/* deps already required at top of daemon.js.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-12T11:14:39.227Z"}
{"evt":"knowledge_added","id":"note-mqatxdyv38f","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","item":"lib/ already establishes the pattern (pure logic in modules, daemon.js is the HTTP shell). routes/ should mirror it. Source edits to daemon.js are GATED and NOT in the orch-gate allowlist - worker must start_task to claim before editing.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-12T11:14:39.227Z"}
