{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqatxdyv38f","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Daemon route split module boundaries and ctx shell architecture","summary":"Decided the seam for splitting daemon.js (3535 lines): daemon.js keeps the outer shell (URL parse, the centralized prefix-based auth gate, sweeps, dispatch, final static + 404 fall-through) and builds ONE ctx object passed to each route module. Modules live in routes/, export (ctx) => (p, m, req, res, u, body) => boolean, tried in order until one returns true. Behavior preserving and order preserving: a pure mechanical extraction, no logic change. SCOPE = PHASED, leaf groups first (user call 2026-06-12): extract meta, graph, task, overlay, git, judge, analytics, onboard, session, ui modules NOW; LEAVE the entangled execution cluster (loop, next-action, route, agent, agents and the decideAll / applyOptimize / sweep* helper web) in daemon.js for a later Phase 2. Regression gate: test/endpoints.test.js plus context-gate-route.test.js must stay green.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-12T11:14:39.223Z","vec":[-0.05204169079661369,0.027993028983473778,-0.014579204842448235,-0.08677273988723755,-0.04216160252690315,-0.05651272460818291,-0.010334966704249382,0.09018604457378387,-0.04211266711354256,-0.013865260407328606,-0.0238077100366354,0.006554826628416777,0.0038643833249807358,-0.03196167200803757,0.07649201154708862,0.012514113448560238,-0.0026147381868213415,0.02367183193564415,0.0074166241101920605,-0.04543294012546539,0.015501453541219234,0.04054497182369232,0.005981017369776964,-0.014897835440933704,-0.09880160540342331,0.007583785802125931,0.0077758729457855225,-0.03092365898191929,0.029092218726873398,-0.03604137897491455,0.09444976598024368,0.07377775013446808,-0.17164161801338196,0.006012041121721268,0.01661875657737255,0.10792509466409683,-0.0013148715952411294,-0.0514933280646801,-0.08780404180288315,-0.04436813294887543,0.120552659034729,0.04663942754268646,0.02578934282064438,-